## Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **REPL** | Read-Eval-Print Loop — a program that reads input, evaluates it, prints the result, and repeats |
| **Singleton** | A design pattern where only one instance of an object is ever created |
| **Guard clause** | A condition check at the top of a function that exits early if preconditions aren't met |
| **Fail fast** | Crashing immediately with a clear error rather than silently producing wrong results |
| **Variable shadowing** | When an inner-scope variable has the same name as an outer-scope one, hiding it |
| **Nullish coalescing (`??`)** | Returns the right-hand value only if left is `null` or `undefined` — not `0` or `""` |
| **ESM (`"type":"module"`)** | ES Module mode — requires `import`/`export` syntax; `__dirname` and `require` are not available |
| **`import.meta.url`** | ESM replacement for `__filename` — gives the URL of the current module file |
| **Destructured defaults** | Setting fallback values inside function parameter destructuring: `{ key = defaultValue }` |
| **Abstraction layer** | A module that wraps complex/third-party logic so the rest of the app doesn't need to know the details |
| **System instruction** | A privileged prompt sent to the Gemini API that defines the model's persona/rules (separate from user content) |
| **Context window** | The total amount of text (tokens) the model can "see" at once — prompt + history + response |
| **RLHF** | Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback — post-training that makes models helpful, sometimes overriding format instructions |
| **Response priming** | Giving the model a partial start to its own response so it completes in a specific format |
| **Model-turn prefill** | Injecting a partial `role:'model'` turn at the end of a `contents` array to prime the response |
| **Multi-turn `contents`** | Passing `[{role:'user',...},{role:'model',...}]` to represent a conversation instead of a plain string |
| **State bleed** | When context or data from a previous agent execution carries over to the next session. Prevented by calling `clear()` on session startup. |
| **Dynamic date injection** | Dynamically appending today's actual calendar date to system instructions so the model correctly reasons about time-sensitive searches. |
| **Token budget management** | Strategically truncating or trimming large payloads to prevent model context window overflow or high costs. |
| **Context Engineering** | Dynamically composing the system prompt from live agent state so it adapts to what the agent has already done. |
| **Research Brief** | A section of the system prompt summarising the agent's current findings to prevent re-searching covered topics. |
| **Deduplication Guard** | A hard-stop instruction telling the model it cannot repeat a search it has already performed. |
| **Urgency Notice** | A mandatory instruction injected near the end of the step budget forcing the model to stop calling tools and write a Final Answer. |
| **Mirrored constant** | A constant defined in two files that must stay in sync — changing one requires changing both. |
